### Codebase Checks

- Measured on DuckDB 1.5.4: `signal.alarm(2)` with its default action ended a process 2.03 s into a `CREATE INDEX ... USING HNSW` that takes 10.4 s on its own. The exit code was -14 (SIGALRM). Another process waiting on the same `fcntl.flock` got the lock 2.03 s after the alarm was set. So the time limit can end the process during the build, which an interrupt cannot do (fourth run).
